# How to cite this software. The README's "Citation and references" section
# lists the papers behind each method mixmogam implements and the provenance
# of the real-data panel it bundles; cite those alongside this entry.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "mixmogam: super-efficient mixed linear models for genome-wide association mapping"
authors:
  - name: "mixmogam contributors"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bvilhjal/mixmogam"
url: "https://github.com/bvilhjal/mixmogam#readme"
keywords:
  - gwas
  - mixed linear model
  - association mapping
  - heritability
  - statistical genetics
abstract: >-
  mixmogam fits mixed linear models for genome-wide association mapping of
  quantitative traits and, with HRATT, case-control outcomes and
  sampling-weighted samples, with leave-one-chromosome-out testing by
  default. It provides an exact EMMAX-style REML path, BOLT-LMM-style
  infinitesimal and two-Gaussian mixture fits, and HRATT, a cross-fitted
  two-step test inspired by LDAK-KVIK. The core uses NumPy and SciPy, with
  optional Numba kernels. The two-step paths are research implementations
  with documented departures from the original programs, and passing input,
  numerical-equivalence and performance checks does not establish scientific
  calibration.
